{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39471942",
      "title": "Scroll-based Animations",
      "sourceHash": "9c482b25a01b78b99fb145d22e6929cd5221c52c1de12599d250229416e88aba",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "Now, to conclude this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 5.163,
          "en": "let's go back to the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "where we have this hero standing in front of the skyline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 11.043,
          "en": "and this 'get started' button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "Now of course this is just a dummy page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "but at the moment it's very boring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 19.65,
          "en": "And to make it less boring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.65,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "I want to add some animations to this hero image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 25.59,
          "en": "and to this whole area at the start of this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "And I want to add a nice parallax, in fact,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "which simply means that these different images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "should move at different speeds as we scroll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "to create a good looking, nice effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "And that's also pretty straightforward to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 43.443,
          "en": "with Framer Motion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.76,
          "end": 47.97,
          "en": "Now for that, we need to go to the page's directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.97,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "and there to the welcome.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 54.723,
          "en": "because that's where all this welcome screen code lives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.22,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "And in there, I now want to animate this div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 63.9,
          "en": "this image, and this image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 67.443,
          "en": "depending on how far the user scrolled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "So therefore, as a first step to animate this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "and the two images, we must import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "from Framer Motion, and that something, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 84.92,
          "en": "is this motion here to create those motion components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.34,
          "end": 88.983,
          "en": "So a motion div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.059,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "And then also two motion images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 98.283,
          "en": "Because otherwise we won't be able to animate these things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 104.838,
          "en": "But now the tricky thing will be to derive the actual values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.838,
          "end": 107.10300000000001,
          "en": "we want to animate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 112.35300000000001,
          "en": "Because now we don't have hard coded animation values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.525,
          "end": 117.45,
          "en": "we can set animate y to a fixed value, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.45,
          "end": 122.4,
          "en": "because this value should change as the user scrolls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.4,
          "end": 123.903,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "And therefore, instead of setting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "to hard coded values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 133.59,
          "en": "we need a way of finding out how far the user scrolled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.59,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "And we need to translate that information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "to animation values we want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 141.333,
          "en": "on this div and those images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.1,
          "end": 146.76,
          "en": "And this is, again, super simple to do with Framer Motion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.76,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "because it gives us two very useful hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 151.593,
          "en": "that help with this task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 155.913,
          "en": "The first hook is to use scroll hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "This hook will help us listen to scroll events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 164.043,
          "en": "and find out how far the user scrolled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "The second important hook is to use transport hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "which will allow us to transform values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 176.373,
          "en": "to values we can use in animations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "For example, values you get from scrolling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "to values we can use to animate the movement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 185.403,
          "en": "along the y axis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 189.21,
          "en": "So we need these two hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.21,
          "end": 191.313,
          "en": "and I'll now show you how to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.57,
          "end": 195.873,
          "en": "We'll start by using use scroll.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 199.29,
          "en": "This will return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 199.29,
          "end": 202.41,
          "en": "with a couple of useful properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 206.61,
          "en": "For example, the scrollY property to tell us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.61,
          "end": 209.37,
          "en": "by how many pixels the user scrolled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.37,
          "end": 211.083,
          "en": "along the vertical axis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.52,
          "end": 215.82,
          "en": "We also have scrollX for the horizontal axis,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.82,
          "end": 218.4,
          "en": "and we have progress properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.4,
          "end": 221.73,
          "en": "to get a relative scrolling value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 224.79,
          "en": "So a value between zero and one, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "where one would mean that the user scrolled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 229.23,
          "en": "all the way to the bottom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 229.23,
          "end": 232.233,
          "en": "and zero means the user didn't scroll at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 238.94,
          "en": "But here, I want to get the absolute pixels with scrollY.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "And now these pixels should be translated to values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 245.583,
          "en": "we can use for the animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 251.07,
          "en": "And let's maybe start by animating some opacity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.07,
          "end": 254.1,
          "en": "before we start moving elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 254.1,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "Because starting with opacity and transporting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "this scroll value to opacity values makes understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 265.14,
          "en": "this use transform hook a little bit easier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 265.14,
          "end": 266.343,
          "en": "in my experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 270.69,
          "en": "So let's say that we want to make this city image here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 275.69,
          "en": "more and more transparent as the user scrolls along,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 276.24,
          "end": 279.603,
          "en": "so then after awhile it is totally transparent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 284.13,
          "en": "To achieve this, you must set the animate prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 284.13,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "and then the opacity, and now we need a value of zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 293.36,
          "en": "once we scrolled far enough and a value of one initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 293.43,
          "end": 294.723,
          "en": "so that it's visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 295.71,
          "end": 299.88,
          "en": "Hence, we need to transform scrollY to one and zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 299.88,
          "end": 304.23,
          "en": "and all the values in between as we are scrolling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.23,
          "end": 306.933,
          "en": "And that's what use transform does for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 307.83,
          "end": 311.79,
          "en": "Use transform takes a value that should be transformed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.79,
          "end": 314.1,
          "en": "so scrollY in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 314.1,
          "end": 316.713,
          "en": "the number of pixels the user scrolled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 317.88,
          "end": 321.15,
          "en": "Then as a second value, it will take an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.15,
          "end": 326.15,
          "en": "of break points, you could say, and as a third value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 326.67,
          "end": 328.92,
          "en": "an array of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 328.92,
          "end": 332.67,
          "en": "Those break points and the values between those break points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 332.67,
          "end": 334.263,
          "en": "should be transformed too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 335.67,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "So let's start with the break points.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 340.53,
          "en": "Keep in mind that this here scrollY",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 340.53,
          "end": 343.503,
          "en": "will be the number of pixels the user scrolled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 344.7,
          "end": 346.62,
          "en": "Initially that will be zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 346.62,
          "end": 349.053,
          "en": "if we start at the top of the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 350.79,
          "end": 354.69,
          "en": "But at some point, we might have scrolled by 200 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 354.69,
          "end": 356.67,
          "en": "along the vertical axis,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 356.67,
          "end": 359.553,
          "en": "so we scrolled down 200 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.48,
          "end": 364.56,
          "en": "Now we might want to translate these pixel values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 368.4,
          "en": "to an opacity of one initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 368.4,
          "end": 372.921,
          "en": "so that this city image is fully visible initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 372.921,
          "end": 375.84,
          "en": "when we haven't scrolled at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 375.84,
          "end": 378.63,
          "en": "And then maybe a opacity of .5,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 378.63,
          "end": 381.78,
          "en": "so that it has a transparency of 50%.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381.78,
          "end": 386.58299999999997,
          "en": "It's 50% transparent after we scroll 200 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 387.51,
          "end": 389.73,
          "en": "And Framer Motion will automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 389.73,
          "end": 392.073,
          "en": "interpolate between those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 393,
          "end": 395.46,
          "en": "And that's how use transform is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.46,
          "end": 399.39300000000003,
          "en": "to transform these pixel values to opacity values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 400.71,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "You're also not limited to two values here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 407.13,
          "en": "We could add a third break point of 300",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 407.13,
          "end": 410.433,
          "en": "and a fourth and last break point of 500.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 411.69,
          "end": 414.75,
          "en": "Now, we also should add some matching values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 414.75,
          "end": 417.36,
          "en": "in this transformation array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 417.36,
          "end": 420.3,
          "en": "And we could say that after 300 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 420.3,
          "end": 423.063,
          "en": "we still want to have an opacity of .5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 424.26,
          "end": 428.85,
          "en": "So as the user continues scrolling after 200 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 428.85,
          "end": 432.483,
          "en": "of scrolling down, the opacity will not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 433.65,
          "end": 437.375,
          "en": "However, if we then add a last value of zero here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 437.375,
          "end": 440.49,
          "en": "this means that after 300 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 440.49,
          "end": 443.58,
          "en": "all the way up to 500 pixels of scrolling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 443.58,
          "end": 447.69,
          "en": "the opacity will change from .5 to zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 447.69,
          "end": 450.093,
          "en": "which means that the item will be transparent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 451.32,
          "end": 454.05,
          "en": "That's how we can transform values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 454.05,
          "end": 459.05,
          "en": "and use transform then returns the transformed value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 459.57,
          "end": 462.18,
          "en": "Though it actually wraps this in a so-called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 462.18,
          "end": 466.35,
          "en": "motion value object so that it does not re-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 466.35,
          "end": 469.47,
          "en": "this component function every time we scroll,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 469.47,
          "end": 473.64,
          "en": "but instead manages this transformed value behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 473.64,
          "end": 477.24,
          "en": "without causing the component function to re-render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 477.24,
          "end": 480.24,
          "en": "So that this entire animation does not impact",
